sequenceDiagram
  title Checking in at the door
  actor S as Student
  actor C as Coordinator
  participant Q as Check-in page (phone camera)
  participant API as POST /api/v1/events/:id/checkin
  participant CI as Check-in service
  participant D as PostgreSQL

  S->>C: Shows QR ticket
  C->>Q: Points the camera at it
  Q->>Q: jsqr reads the code from camera frames
  Q->>API: ticketCode
  API->>API: requireEventStaff: signed in, and manages this event
  API->>CI: checkIn(actor, eventId, ticketCode, now)
  CI->>CI: Verify the signature, without touching the database
  alt Signature is wrong
    CI-->>Q: 404 INVALID_TICKET
    Q-->>C: Red card: not a valid ticket
  else Signature is right
    CI->>D: UPDATE registration SET checked_in_at WHERE confirmed AND not checked in
    alt One row changed
      CI->>D: INSERT audit_logs entry
      CI-->>Q: 200, person and counts
      Q-->>C: Green card: name, photo, roll number, team
    else No row changed (already scanned on another phone)
      CI-->>Q: 409 ALREADY_CHECKED_IN, who and when
      Q-->>C: Amber card: don't let them in twice
    end
  end
  Note over Q,D: If the camera fails, typing the code or searching by name uses the same service
